Yes. It really was.

> I like your idea for these song effects much better.  Would using one of
> these abilities drain mana just like casting a spell?

Yes. The idea is the songs have something of magical.

> Would a bard character know them all, or learn some of them as he
> increases in level?

The second choice. The simpler ones (sleep and fear, for example) could be
available from the start; others will appear in the menu when the bard
gains levels. I thought of mantaining the music skill, so other songs
will be available not at a specific xplvl, but when he reaches 'skilled'
and 'expert'. 
And maybe some of the songs could have different effects depending on the
skill... for example: singing Fear with basic skill could scare only
insects (idea still shamelessly copied from AD&D bard song...), and with
higher skill it will try to scare every monster in range. This is just an
example, I didn't thought of any good effect.

Mantaining the music skill also have the advantage of letting other
classes use songs (not sure if this is a Good Thing or unbalancing...)

> If the former, would there be a chance of failure for the more powerful
> effects while the bard is still low-level?

I thought of throwing away the idea of failure chance, and let the
monsters try resist the song effects (much like the way they resist spells
and wands). So, a bard can just play the Sleep song normally, but if the
monsters will really sleep it's up to them ;-) Naturally the chance of
they sleeping will be a function of the music skill, dexterity and
charisma.

>  Finally, would the type of instrument and whether or not it's magical
> play into the success rate?

Initially I thought this was a nice idea. But if the bard wants the magic
instrument to generate its common effect (such using a horn of fire to
spit fire), how the best approach? Just let him improvise? Because of
this, I thought of imposing the restriction that magic instruments would
not be usable to play the bard's songs -- after all, they're instruments
instilled with magic to perform certain actions (that normally non-bards
can do by just playing them, even with no knowledge of music). So when the
bard uses a magic instrument, and if enough skilled, s|he can control the
instrument's effects; for example, when playing a fire horn while skilled
in music, it can spit a (tame) flaming sphere (I liked so much the idea of
creating flaming/freezing spheres that I don't want to throw it away
easily). More details below.

> Personally, I the bard knowing all of his powers, but having 100%
> failure rates for many of them until he gets higher-level, and his
> chance of success being influenced by the type and quality of the
> instrument (e.g. magical instruments increase chance of success; pacify
> works better with a harp, panic with drums, etc.).

Yes, but the failure rate will be calculated for each monster, depending
of it resisting the song or not. So we won't see in the song menu: "sleep
- 40% failure". You will know you can play a song, but will not know its
effects; if some of the monsters around you are too high level or MR, the
song will have no effect on them.

Below is a list of the songs, as I'm thinking now:

Song                Req.skill  Instruments
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Pacify              unskilled  harp, syrinx
Sleep               unskilled  flute, syrinx
Paralyse               expert  flute
Fear                unskilled  horn, drum
Confusion               basic  horn
Friendship(taming)    skilled  harp
Berserk Allies          basic  bugle, drum
Calm Down Allies        basic  syrinx

The syrinx is the reed flute of satyrs (they always carry one). This
gives the bard a chance of finding another instrument, since it's a
little rare finding musical instruments in nethack.


When playing magic instruments:

- horn fire/frost(skilled): generate tame spheres.
- horn plenty(skilled): can choose what it will produce.
- drum earthquake(skilled): collapse the dungeon's ceiling, creating
  boulders/rocks.
- magic harp(skilled): normal effects & calm shopkeepers
  (at expert,tame humans?)
- magic flute: no ideas. Just increase chance of sleeping?


